  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "This deep colored cultivar has very deep purple-red foliage, almost black red. The color holds well into late summer, especially if the plant is given afternoon shade. In the fall, crimson tones dominate. The fiveor seven-lobed leaves are 7-8 cm long and 8-9 cm wide, with the lobes spreading openly. The leaves are rather thin in texture. The lobes are elongate-ovate, terminating in a slender point, and they divide to within 1 cm of the leaf base. The margins are regularly and lightly serrated. The slender red-brown petioles are 4 cm long. The leaves are spaced openly along the shoots, giving the appearance of less foliage than normal. The growth tivars to signify the color red. This cultivar has also been known under the names"
  },
